        <headline>Coastal Flood Advisory issued September 24 at 9:08PM EDT until September 26 at 11:00AM EDT by NWS Upton NY</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...One to two feet of inundation above ground level
expected in vulnerable areas near the waterfront and shoreline.

* WHERE...In New Jersey, Eastern Bergen County. In New York, New
York (Manhattan) County.

* WHEN...From 6 PM Friday to 11 AM EDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in the more vulnerable locations near
the waterfront and shoreline. Some roads and low lying properties
including parking lots, parks, lawns, and homes and businesses with
basements near the waterfront will experience minor flooding.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Localized moderate coastal flooding
possible Friday night into early Saturday.
</description>
        <instruction>If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be
closed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of
unknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone
property.</instruction>
